(6667029, 996034, 18450, '<td valign="top">Fun image, I love it!!</td>', 'Fun image, I love it!!', '2012-02-08 04:16:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667125, 995887, 12611, '<td valign="top">I think you way you integrated the dog into the shot is masterful, child-like, yet a shoulder to lean on, (literally in fact)- the processing is terrific, especially the outlining of dog''s ear and eye- a counterpoint to the grainy glowing resonance of the human face.</td>', 'I think you way you integrated the dog into the shot is masterful, child-like, yet a shoulder to lean on, (literally in fact)- the processing is terrific, especially the outlining of dog''s ear and eye- a counterpoint to the grainy glowing resonance of the human face.', '2012-02-08 08:14:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667295, 995686, 135196, '<td valign="top">After reading the tutorial I find it an amazing work. Congrats!</td>', 'After reading the tutorial I find it an amazing work. Congrats!', '2012-02-08 11:23:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667511, 996023, 143979, '<td valign="top">Love this shot. Well done!</td>', 'Love this shot. Well done!', '2012-02-08 16:06:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667543, 995615, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings fromt the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I had the feeling that this was one of your shots and that I might be critiquing it!  Like that you''re in profile and cat is more face-on to the camera.  The b/w seems to enhabce the feeling you wanted to get, and glad that you didn''t go over the top with a ''witchy'' outfit.  That the cat is black and white only helps break up the stereotype of a black cat as a witch''s familiar.<br/> <br/>Not so sure about the crop, but hard to see what else might have worked.  The high-key lighting seems to work fairly well, and kitty doesn''t look too upset at being cast in the role you''ve given her!  It''s always a lot of fun to critique your images, keep them coming.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings fromt the Critique Club! I had the feeling that this was one of your shots and that I might be critiquing it!  Like that you''re in profile and cat is more face-on to the camera.  The b/w seems to enhabce the feeling you wanted to get, and glad that you didn''t go over the top with a ''witchy'' outfit.  That the cat is black and white only helps break up the stereotype of a black cat as a witch''s familiar. Not so sure about the crop, but hard to see what else might have worked.  The high-key lighting seems to work fairly well, and kitty doesn''t look too upset at being cast in the role you''ve given her!  It''s always a lot of fun to critique your images, keep them coming. Feel free to PM me, Susan', '2012-02-08 16:53:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667554, 995847, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Love the rattie''s posture and catchlight in the eye as she tenderly grooms her co-owner.  Good use of b/w and the gentleness of the hands shows through; don''t need to see a face to see that this is a loving and mutual relationship.  Lighting is very good, comp is a little on the safe side but this finished 20th, so not that objectionable :-)  I was a little puzzled by the squiggly thing but realize now it must be Dione''s tail.  Glad to see that it healed well!  Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Love the rattie''s posture and catchlight in the eye as she tenderly grooms her co-owner.  Good use of b/w and the gentleness of the hands shows through; don''t need to see a face to see that this is a loving and mutual relationship.  Lighting is very good, comp is a little on the safe side but this finished 20th, so not that objectionable :-)  I was a little puzzled by the squiggly thing but realize now it must be Dione''s tail.  Glad to see that it healed well!  Keep up the good work. Feel free to PM me, Susan', '2012-02-08 16:59:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667616, 995619, 127537, '<td valign="top">I''ve shared my life with 2 dalmatians in the last 25 years - couldn''t fail to love this photo.  Sure makes me miss Pepper &amp; Tess</td>', 'I''ve shared my life with 2 dalmatians in the last 25 years - couldn''t fail to love this photo.  Sure makes me miss Pepper & Tess', '2012-02-08 18:06:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667759, 996023, 8759, '<td valign="top">Well done. Also. Congrats on top photo taken with iPhone 4s!!!</td>', 'Well done. Also. Congrats on top photo taken with iPhone 4s!!!', '2012-02-08 20:42:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6667773, 995619, 79720, '<td valign="top">Love it, Nick! What a character...the both of you!</td>', 'Love it, Nick! What a character...the both of you!', '2012-02-08 21:01:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6668290, 995983, 68947, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by slickchik:</b></div><hr/><i> So is it a nebelung? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry...I forgot that you''d asked that question.  No, she''s a "mutt".  She was a ferral cat that we got as a kitten.  I have no clue what she really is and it seems the vets don''t either.  She had the oddest of fur when we first got her...these stray long white, scraggly things.  She looked part raccoon back then LOL.  She''s becoming more beautiful as she gets older. :)  Thank you for taking the time to ask. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by slickchik: So is it a nebelung?   Sorry...I forgot that you''d asked that question.  No, she''s a "mutt".  She was a ferral cat that we got as a kitten.  I have no clue what she really is and it seems the vets don''t either.  She had the oddest of fur when we first got her...these stray long white, scraggly things.  She looked part raccoon back then LOL.  She''s becoming more beautiful as she gets older. :)  Thank you for taking the time to ask. :)', '2012-02-09 13:06:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6668724, 995710, 67697, '<td valign="top">This reminds me of a photo I took, except it was me throwing a stick at my boys lol.  I always enjoy the tones you pull out of your shots.  Great action capture.  Congrats on 2nd place!</td>', 'This reminds me of a photo I took, except it was me throwing a stick at my boys lol.  I always enjoy the tones you pull out of your shots.  Great action capture.  Congrats on 2nd place!', '2012-02-09 23:52:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6668726, 995835, 67697, '<td valign="top">I have a cat and I can''t imagine getting him to sit still, let alone wear a dress.  This is hilarious.  Congrats on 10th place!</td>', 'I have a cat and I can''t imagine getting him to sit still, let alone wear a dress.  This is hilarious.  Congrats on 10th place!', '2012-02-09 23:54:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6668727, 995718, 67697, '<td valign="top">Anita, I love the direction your shots have been taking.  It is quite apparent that you have been emotionally inspired.  This is great and love the toning.  Congrats on a great finish!</td>', 'Anita, I love the direction your shots have been taking.  It is quite apparent that you have been emotionally inspired.  This is great and love the toning.  Congrats on a great finish!', '2012-02-09 23:55:19.000000', NULL, 0);
